<!--
  presentation-watchdog.plist.template -- ready-to-apply, NOT installed.
  Named Stop: installation is a live production change (Super Spec 9.9.2 and 5.3).

  PLACEHOLDERS to replace before installing:
    1. <WATCHDOG_SCRIPT_PATH>  -- absolute path to presentation-watchdog.sh
    2. <SCAN_ROOT>             -- the root directory to scan for run dirs
                                 (os.pathsep-packed for multiple roots)
    3. <LOG_PATH>              -- where stdout/stderr should go. This SAME
                                 path is passed as argv[2]: the script tees
                                 its own diagnostics into it, so the launchd
                                 log and the script's log are one file.
    4. <NOTIFY_CMD>            -- the PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD transport argv
                                 (shlex-parseable), e.g.
                                 <SCRIPTS_DIR>/presentation-notify.py.
                                 FIX 49: with the script's fail-closed gate
                                 (FIX 22) this is MANDATORY -- an unset
                                 transport makes every tick exit 4
                                 (AF-NOTIFY-UNCONFIGURED) before any pass
                                 runs, which is exactly the "watchdog never
                                 scans" state this plist exists to prevent.
    5. <OWNER_CHAT_ID>         -- the operator's NUMERIC Telegram chat id
                                 (FIX 64: launchd runs this job with no
                                 environment, so subsystem alerts -- watchdog
                                 stall / supervisor alarm / capacity
                                 UNDETERMINED -- carry only their subsystem
                                 NAME as the chat id. OWNER_CHAT_ID is the
                                 resolution key both report.dispatch3 and
                                 presentation-notify.py read; without it a
                                 stall alert can never land in the operator
                                 chat. Strongly recommended -- the tick's
                                 --sweep-undeliverable-roots pass retries
                                 unsent alerts, but only this variable makes
                                 them deliverable.)

  FIX 19 (MASTER Part 8): every tick of this job now also runs the stray
  orphan reaper -- process_reaper.py --scan-root <SCAN_ROOT> -- after the
  sweep-undeliverable pass. It reaps build-shaped strays (dispatcher,
  prompt-wave workers, render children; argv patterns cover both the script
  and the `-m` module forms) whose run dir is terminal/stale/gone, children
  included. A live run's processes classify REAL_BUILD and are never
  touched, so the pass is safe every tick. The documented rollback is an
  EnvironmentVariables entry:
      <key>PRESENTATION_REAPER_DISABLE</key>
      <string>1</string>
  which makes the tick skip the reaper pass entirely (for a box debugging
  its own process table with the reaper out of the way).

  PATH (FIX 49): launchd starts this job with NO inherited environment --
  no /opt/homebrew/bin and no npm-global bin -- so gtimeout and the
  `openclaw` gateway CLI (the transport's send path) are invisible to it.
  The EnvironmentVariables PATH below is the minimal live PATH that fixes
  both; it is templated as a placeholder so a box with a different
  prefix layout substitutes its own rather than inheriting a wrong one.

  Install (Named Stop -- do not run unattended):
    cp presentation-watchdog.plist.template ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.presentations.watchdog.plist
    Replace every placeholder above in the installed copy.
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.presentations.watchdog.plist

  Uninstall (Named Stop -- do not run unattended):
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.presentations.watchdog.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.presentations.watchdog.plist

  Verify it is running:
    launchctl list | grep com.presentations.watchdog
-->
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.presentations.watchdog</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>&lt;WATCHDOG_SCRIPT_PATH&gt;</string>
        <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SCAN_ROOT</key>
        <string>&lt;SCAN_ROOT&gt;</string>
        <key>GRACE</key>
        <string>1.5</string>
        <key>SCAN_DEPTH</key>
        <string>3</string>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>&lt;WATCHDOG_PATH&gt;</string>
        <key>PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD</key>
        <string>&lt;NOTIFY_CMD&gt;</string>
        <key>OWNER_CHAT_ID</key>
        <string>&lt;OWNER_CHAT_ID&gt;</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>600</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
</dict>
</plist>
